      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BONNY IMPACT (2) found the right race, and after find the front early on, she was too good, scoring by over a length. She slips down a grade for this, and an extra 1.5kg should not be enough to stop her from repeating the dose. MISS TOP GUN (1) has been racing fairly well since being bought out of Victoria, and she will be facing her easiest assignment since moving to this State. She has a good gate, and should go close to winning this. GO GO DOLLY (7) needed her fresh up run here 3 weeks ago, and the travelling Kym Healy stable will have her fit second up. Include in all combos in a modest contest. PUB CRAWL (5) drops back to 1000m and that could be the key to him finding some form again. He benefits from a 2kg claim, and is worth one more chance. OUR SQUAMOSA (6) resumes from a spell, and though she usually needs a run, she can give a field like this a decent shake. Check the markets.",
